"ACPErrorSSHHostKeyChangedDetail" -> "This can mean that someone is intercepting the connection, or that the server was reinstalled. Check the new key with the server's administrator before you change your known_hosts file.",
"ACPErrorSSHAuthFailed" -> "`host` didn't accept your SSH key.",
"ACPErrorSSHAuthFailedDetail" -> "Agent chats sign in without prompts: use a key that is loaded in your SSH agent or has no passphrase, and give its file with \"Arguments\" -> {\"-i\", \"path\"} in the \"SSHSettings\" setting if it is not a default key.",
